{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan an Nasai","section":{"5":{"eng-name":"The Book of Salah","ara-name":"كتاب الصلاة"}},"section_detail":{"5":{"hadithnumber_first":448,"hadithnumber_last":493,"arabicnumber_first":448,"arabicnumber_last":493}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":474,"arabicnumber":474,"text":"Rapporté par Abu Qilabah : Abu Al-Malih m’a raconté : \"Nous étions avec Buraidah un jour nuageux et il a dit : 'Priez tôt, car le Messager d’Allah (ﷺ) a dit : \"Celui qui abandonne la prière du ‘Asr, ses bonnes actions seront perdues","grades":[{"name":"Abu Ghuddah","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari"}],"reference":{"book":5,"hadith":27},"chapter":{"id":15,"ara-name":"باب مَنْ تَرَكَ صَلاَةَ الْعَصْرِ .","eng-name":"One Who Abandons Salat Al-'Asr","isFirstHadith":true}}]}